course: dictionary
lesson: 4342
title: Making a good guess
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: To guess means to give an answer when you are not sure and do not know all the facts. A guess is that answer. «Prefixes let you guess new words.» You can make a good guess at a new word's meaning by looking at its parts, but a guess can be wrong, so check it.
explain: Guessing is useful in maths and science. In maths, guess and check (trial and improvement) means you try an answer, see how far off it is, and then try again. In science, a hypothesis is a careful guess that you test to find out if it is right.
explain: «I guess» in everyday talk means «I think» or «I suppose». «Children often hear bits of grown-up money talk and imagine the worst; asking a parent is usually less scary than guessing.» Here guessing means filling the gaps with a made-up answer, which may be wrong.
fact: To guess means to give an answer when you are not sure, without knowing all the facts.
fact: A guess is the answer you give; to guess right means to find the right answer by guessing.
fact: «I guess» in everyday talk means «I think» or «I suppose».
fact: «Some pictures, like the duck-rabbit, can be seen in two ways, which shows that seeing is partly guessing.»
fact: Useful phrases: make a guess, take a guess, a good guess, a wild guess, guess what, guess and check.
exercise: «Stories grow because people fill gaps with guesses.» What does guesses mean here? | *Answers given without knowing all the facts | Long, careful sums | Answers checked by a teacher | Pictures drawn in a book
exercise: In maths, what is guess and check? | Never changing an answer once it is written | *Trying an answer, seeing how far off it is, then trying again | Copying the answer from the back of the book | Adding numbers in your head only
exercise: Ben says, «I guess it will rain today.» What does I guess mean here? | I am going to sing | I know for certain | Stop! | *I think
exercise: «Ratings are decided by trained examiners who follow published rules, not by guessing.» What does the sentence tell us? | *Ratings are not decided by guessing | Ratings are decided by guessing | Rules are never published | Film makers decide ratings by guessing
test: In science, what is a hypothesis? | *A careful guess that is tested | A fact that can never change | A sum with no answer | A kind of picture
test: Which sentence uses guess to mean «I think»? | Guess the word, then write it down. | Write a guess on the board. | Make a guess at the answer and check it. | *I guess we should set off soon.
exam: «Children often hear bits of grown-up money talk and imagine the worst; asking a parent is usually less scary than guessing.» According to the sentence, what is usually less scary? | Imagining the worst | *Asking a parent | Guessing about money talk | Hearing bits of grown-up talk
